www.realclearpolling.com\/polls\/senate\/general\/2024\/maine\/king-vs-kouzounas-vs-costello-vs-cherry\">Senate<\/a><strong><br \/>2022:<\/strong>\u00a0<a href=\"https:\/\/www.realclearpolitics.com\/epolls\/2022\/governor\/me\/maine_governor_lepage_vs_mills-7623.html\">Governor<\/a><strong><br \/>2020:\u00a0<\/strong><a href=\"https:\/\/www.realclearpolitics.com\/epolls\/2020\/president\/me\/maine_trump_vs_biden-6922.html\">President<\/a>\u00a0|\u00a0<a href=\"https:\/\/www.realclearpolitics.com\/epolls\/2020\/president\/mecd2\/maine_cd2_trump_vs_biden-7215.html\">CD2<\/a>\u00a0|\u00a0<a href=\"https:\/\/www.realclearpolling.com\/polls\/senate\/general\/2020\/maine\/collins-vs-gideon\">Senate<\/a> |\u00a0<a href=\"https:\/\/www.realclearpolitics.com\/epolls\/2020\/house\/me\/maine_2nd_district_crafts_vs_golden-7125.html\">ME-2<\/a><strong><br \/>2018:<\/strong>\u00a0<a href=\"https:\/\/www.realclearpolitics.com\/epolls\/2018\/governor\/me\/maine_governor_moody_vs_mills-6643.html\">Governor<\/a>\u00a0|\u00a0<a href=\"https:\/\/www.realclearpolitics.com\/epolls\/2018\/senate\/me\/maine_senate_brakey_vs_king-6266.html\">Senate<\/a>\u00a0|\u00a0<a href=\"https:\/\/www.realclearpolitics.com\/epolls\/2018\/house\/me\/maine_2nd_district_poliquin_vs_golden-6341.html\">ME-2<\/a><strong><br \/>2016:<span>\u00a0<\/span><\/strong><a href=\"https:\/\/www.realclearpolitics.com\/epolls\/2016\/president\/me\/maine_trump_vs_clinton_vs_johnson_vs_stein-6091.html\">President<\/a>\u00a0|\u00a0<a href=\"https:\/\/www.realclearpolitics.com\/epolls\/2016\/president\/mecd1\/maine_cd1_trump_vs_clinton_vs_johnson_vs_stein-6135.html\">CD1<\/a><span>\u00a0<\/span>|\u00a0<a href=\"https:\/\/www.realclearpolitics.com\/epolls\/2016\/president\/mecd2\/maine_cd2_trump_vs_clinton_vs_johnson_vs_stein-6127.html\">CD2<\/a><span>\u00a0<\/span>|\u00a0<a href=\"http:\/\/www.realclearpolitics.com\/epolls\/2016\/house\/me\/maine_1st_district_holbrook_vs_pingree-6132.html\">ME-1<\/a><span>\u00a0<\/span>|\u00a0<a href=\"https:\/\/www.realclearpolitics.com\/epolls\/2016\/house\/me\/maine_2nd_district_poliquin_vs_cain-6028.html\">ME-2<\/a><strong><br \/>2014:\u00a0<\/strong><a href=\"http:\/\/www.realclearpolitics.com\/epolls\/2014\/governor\/me\/maine_governor_lepage_vs_michaud_vs_cutler-3558.html\">Governor<\/a><span>\u00a0<\/span>|\u00a0<a href=\"http:\/\/www.realclearpolitics.com\/epolls\/2014\/senate\/me\/maine_senate_collins_vs_bellows-4168.html\">Senate<\/a>\u00a0|\u00a0<a href=\"http:\/\/www.realclearpolitics.com\/epolls\/latest_polls\/house\/\">ME-2<\/a><strong><br \/><br \/><\/strong><\/p>"},"dataAnalysis":{"title":"Race Analysis","content":"<p>\u201cAs goes Maine, so goes the nation.\u201d This was the rule of thumb for political prognosticators for decades. Maine is a quirky state, and for years it held its elections in September. This gave an early view of the country\u2019s mood before the advent of reliable public opinion polling. But make no mistake:\u00a0For years the only question was how large the Republican candidate\u2019s victory would be. From 1880 until\u00a01954, when Democrat Ed Muskie won, Republicans lost only five gubernatorial elections, even though those elections were held every two years. Since the Civil War, Maine has sent only a handful of Democrats to the Senate; most of its senators have been Republicans, although they have been cut from a decidedly moderate, or even liberal, cloth.<\/p>\n<p>Susan Collins may be the last Republican in that vein. She was elected in 1996 by a close margin and faced races that were at least somewhat competitive until fairly late in the cycle in 2002 and 2008. In 2020, most prognosticators thought that she was in deep trouble\u2014she didn\u2019t lead in a single poll all year\u2014before she wound up winning by almost nine points. Analysts have offered various explanations for that poll miss, but Collins does have a history of overperforming her polls.<\/p>\n<p>Democrats were hopeful this year about the prospects for oysterman and business owner Graham Platner, but his candidacy collapsed amid a flurry of personal scandals and sexual\u00a0assault allegations, which he denied. They replaced Platner in July with former state senator Troy Jackson. Jackson has been an underwhelming candidate, but Democrats counter that in a year like 2026, \u201cnot scandal-tarred\u201d may be all it takes to defeat Collins. Jackson has led in most polling, but Democrats still fear a repeat of Collins\u2019 2020 overperformance.<\/p>"},"showLineChart":1,"showBarChart":1,"showLineChartFirst":1,"sideCharts":{"charts_on_top":0,"left_chart_race_id":"6928","right_chart_race_id":"4168"},"show_final_results":0,"chart_data":{"chart_id":"7657","chart_axis_x":"1","chart_grid_x":"4","chart_axis_y":"1","chart_grid_y":"10","chart_min":"","chart_max":"","chart_start":"1783400400","chart_end":"","poll_id":"9100","chart_highlight":"#bbbb00","chart_days_extend":"7","chart_height":"360","chart_height_mobile":"360","chart_html5":"1","chart_main_percent":"70","chart_spread_percent":"30","chart_spread_range":"10","chart_name_in_tooltips":"1","chart_spread_force_0_y_axis":"1","chart_y_axis_min":null,"chart_y_axis_max":null,"chart_y_axis_min_m":null,"chart_y_axis_max_m":null,"chart_dates":{"7D":"0","14D":"0","30D":"0","MAX":"1"},"chart_dates_old":[{"period":"DD","count":"14","label":"7D","selected":"0"},{"period":"DD","count":"21","label":"14D","selected":"0"},{"period":"DD","count":"37","label":"30D","selected":"0"},{"period":"MAX","count":"1","label":"MAX","selected":"1"}],"chart_dates_mobile":{"7D":"0","14D":"0","30D":"0","MAX":"1"},"chart_dates_mobile_old":[{"period":"DD","count":"14","label":"7D","selected":"0"},{"period":"DD","count":"21","label":"14D","selected":"0"},{"period":"DD","count":"37","label":"30D","selected":"0"},{"period":"MAX","count":"1","label":"MAX","selected":"1"}]}},"poll":[{"id":"9100","type":"rcp_average","pollster":"rcp_average","date":"10\/5 - 10\/26","confidenceInterval":"","samp